      "title": "Imitation of Arm Gestures by the Semi-Humanoid Robot NICO",
      "takeaway": "This method paper presents a gesture-imitation system for the semi-humanoid robot NICO that uses analytical geometry and a pretrained MediaPipe pose-estimation model to convert monocular RGB frames into 3D body landmarks, compute joint angles, and map them to NICO's motor configuration for predefined motion sequences. Preliminary experiments with six participants of different heights across several representative arm gestures show the approach can produce meaningful imitative motions from RGB input alone, while exposing limitations in complex poses and wrist-related movements. When reading, inspect the geometric derivations for joint-angle computation and the mapping strategy to NICO's motor limits, as these determine the system's robustness and scalability to more intricate gestures.",
